1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,933
This is a voice note to a shop's WhatsApp.

2
00:00:03,983 --> 00:00:08,581
Seconds later it's a priced
order with a PayPal link,

3
00:00:08,631 --> 00:00:11,650
and the AI never touched the money.

4
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:16,719
Across East Africa, small shops
already sell in WhatsApp chats.

5
00:00:16,769 --> 00:00:19,485
Orders come as voice notes, and totals,

6
00:00:19,535 --> 00:00:22,819
payment links and stock
are worked out by hand.

7
00:00:22,869 --> 00:00:26,650
Katale AI turns that chat
into the shop's back office.

8
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:30,850
The merchant just talks.

9
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:35,500
The AI understands the request,

10
00:00:35,550 --> 00:00:47,950
but every price and total comes from the
shop's catalogue, computed by the backend.

11
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:59,650
And yes isn't enough: money only moves
on a one-time code bound to this order.

12
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:07,179
The customer pays on
PayPal, here in Sandbox.

13
00:01:07,229 --> 00:01:19,650
A verified webhook marks the order paid,
tells the merchant, and the stock drops.

14
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:28,071
Customers shop on the same
number: browse with photos,

15
00:01:28,121 --> 00:01:33,864
add to a cart and check out with PayPal.

16
00:01:33,914 --> 00:01:43,133
Ask for 500 baskets, and the shop's
rules answer, not the model.

17
00:01:43,183 --> 00:01:49,650
Every cart and total is
built by the backend.

18
00:01:50,300 --> 00:01:53,512
After the sale, the same rule.

19
00:01:53,562 --> 00:02:00,472
The AI prepares the shipment, the
merchant approves with a code,

20
00:02:00,522 --> 00:02:04,714
and the tracking number goes to PayPal.

21
00:02:04,764 --> 00:02:07,650
Disputes work the same way.

22
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:12,216
The dashboard runs on AG Grid.

23
00:02:12,266 --> 00:02:19,619
Edit stock right in the grid,
ask AG Studio for a chart,

24
00:02:19,669 --> 00:02:23,850
and open the trace of any order:

25
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:31,650
the voice note, the AI's decision,
the approval and PayPal.

26
00:02:32,300 --> 00:02:36,918
Under the hood: a WhatsApp worker,
an AI agent with typed tools,

27
00:02:36,968 --> 00:02:39,471
a backend that checks every number,

28
00:02:39,521 --> 00:02:43,191
and PayPal orders, webhooks,
tracking and disputes.

29
00:02:43,241 --> 00:02:44,650
471 automated tests.

30
00:02:45,300 --> 00:02:45,845
AI prepares.

31
00:02:45,895 --> 00:02:46,887
The backend verifies.

32
00:02:46,937 --> 00:02:47,979
The merchant approves.

33
00:02:48,029 --> 00:02:48,772
PayPal executes.

34
00:02:48,822 --> 00:02:51,650
Katale AI, built in Uganda for
sellers across East Africa.
